+## Appointment exports
+
+Open the staff workspace against an existing salon database:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m fernhill --db fernhill.db reports
+```
+
+Visit **http://127.0.0.1:8001/**. Choose From date, To date, and a status, then
+Preview or Download CSV. Both dates are included. The workspace starts with last
+month; shortcuts also select this month or the last 30 days. The preview shows
+50 appointments per page and counts for the selected range/status. Download always
+includes **all matching appointments**, even when viewing a later preview page.
+Download uses the current form values, so you do not have to press Preview first.
+The form and downloads also work without JavaScript.
+
+This is a separate, read-only staff tool. It opens the database in SQLite read-only
+mode, binds only to `127.0.0.1`, and is not part of the public booking app. It rejects
+remote clients, unexpected Host headers, and cross-site browser requests. There is
+no staff login: anyone with access to this computer can use it. Do not expose this
+server through a proxy or use it as a hosted staff portal. `--port 8002` selects a
+different local port; Ctrl+C stops the server.
+
+For a direct export, without opening a browser:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m fernhill --db fernhill.db export --from 2026-09-01 --to 2026-09-30 --output september-appointments.csv
+```
+
+The destination must be a new file; existing files are never overwritten. Omit
+`--output` to write CSV bytes to standard output. A price explanation is printed
+to standard error so it does not contaminate redirected CSV. `--status` accepts
+`all` (default), `booked`, `done`, or `cancelled`. Missing databases are not created.
+
+The CSV has one row per appointment, ordered by start then appointment ID, with
+these columns: `date,start,end,groomer,client,dog,service,price,status`. Dates are
+`YYYY-MM-DD`; times use the salon's local clock, normally `HH:MM`. The filter uses
+the appointment's start date. `done` is shown as Completed in the workspace.
+Cancelled appointments are included by default. An empty range produces column
+headings with no data rows. Contact details and dog notes are not exported.
+
+**Price means the current service catalog price, not the amount charged or paid.**
+Fernhill does not store historical appointment prices, discounts, tips, taxes, or
+payment records. Editing a service's price also changes the price shown for its
+past appointments. Cancelled appointments keep the listed service price. Use this
+as an appointment handoff, not a payment or revenue ledger.
+
+Files use comma delimiters, standard CSV quoting, CRLF row endings, and UTF-8 with
+a byte-order mark so Excel can recognize accented names. Prices are exact decimal
+numbers without currency symbols. Names that start with a spreadsheet formula
+marker (`=`, `+`, `-`, `@`, including after whitespace) or a tab/newline get a leading
+apostrophe to keep them as text. This apostrophe may be visible in some importers.
+If your spreadsheet application does not detect the format, import the file as
+UTF-8 with comma as the separator. Opening and importing in Excel and Google
+Sheets themselves is not part of the automated test suite.
+
+The staff server has its own endpoints: `GET /` for the form/preview and
+`GET /appointments.csv?start=2026-09-01&end=2026-09-30&status=all` for the download.
+Both return `Cache-Control: no-store`. Invalid, missing, or reversed dates return
+a readable HTTP 400 page. These routes are intentionally absent from `serve`.
+
 See [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) for what's next.
